sentences.l:
So having spoken, from the thickets crept out heavenly Odysseus,
from the dense wood a shoot he broke with his stout hand,
of leaves, that he might shield about his skin the genitals of the man.

He set out to go like a mountain-nurtured lion, trusting in his strength,
who goes, rained on and blown on, and in him the eyes
blaze;

If some god you are, of those who the wide heaven hold,
to Artemis you I at least, daughter of great Zeus,
in form and in size and in stature most nearly liken;

But if some one of mortals you are, who upon the earth dwell,
three times blessed indeed for you your father and lady mother,
three times blessed too your brothers;

So in just the same way, that too when I saw I was amazed in my heart
for long, since never yet such a trunk had come up from the earth,
as you, woman, I marvel at and am amazed at, and I fear terribly
to touch your knees;

for you, after many evils toiled through,
first I have come to, and of the others I know no one
of men who this city and land hold.

And to you may the gods give as many things as in your own mind you desire,
a husband and a home, and may they grant like-mindedness
good;

For truly than this nothing is stronger and better
than when of one mind in their thoughts a house they keep,
husband and wife;

There is not this man, a living mortal, nor will there ever be,
who to the land of the Phaeacian men shall come
bringing battle;

So she spoke, and they stopped and called on one another,
and set Odysseus down in the shelter, as ordered
Nausicaa, daughter of great-spirited Alcinous;

“Attendants, stand thus far off, so that I myself
the brine from my shoulders will wash off, and with oil
anoint myself;
